# Normalise line endings so a clone on any OS matches what the tools expect.
#
# This matters most for the generated dataset: docs/DATA_SCHEMA.md specifies LF
# endings, and `python data/generate_dataset.py` writes LF explicitly so the
# output is byte-identical every run. Without this, a Windows clone would get
# CRLF and regenerating would show every line as changed.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.csv text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
*.js text eol=lf
*.jsx text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.css text eol=lf
*.html text eol=lf

*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
